  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Mason Barnett lasted 3.1 innings and the lead they built early in Cleveland evaporated fast.",
    "what_this_means": "They owned the first inning. Gelof hit a two-run homer to center and they were up 3-0 before most games felt awake. Then the fourth inning arrived and everything inverted. Three runs scored on Cleveland's side and suddenly they were chasing instead of leading. The bullpen did its job after that. Blewett threw 1.2 clean, Johnson and Medina combined for two more scoreless frames. But by then the momentum had flipped and stayed flipped. Gelof's three RBIs kept them in it the whole way, but three hits and eight strikeouts across nine innings is not a formula that holds ballgames. They had the game. They didn't keep it. Eight runners left on base. Nothing to show for them.",
    "what_to_watch": "Tanner Bibee arrives tonight with a 4.16 ERA, and Jacob Lopez takes the mound for the Athletics in a game they need to steal back. The series does not wait for the offense to find itself.",
